WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.300
In May 2026,

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.000
Yin Yanliang, the founder of RT-Mart,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.933
passed away at the age of 76

00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:07.733
in a ward at Taipei Veterans General Hospital.

00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:08.533
Meanwhile,

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:09.500
starting in July,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.166
Carrefour, the French giant that had been unrivaled

00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:13.733
in Taiwan for over 30 years

00:00:13.733 --> 00:00:15.566
, would officially remove its signboard.

00:00:15.566 --> 00:00:16.733
A pioneer's curtain call and

00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:18.100
an old brand's departure—

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.233
these two events coincided in the same summer.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.800
If you only see them as

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.200
two separate news stories

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.200
, you've missed

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.833
the most exciting commercial drama

00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:28.633
that has unfolded on this island in the past 30 years.

00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:29.500
In fact,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.533
since the late 1980s,

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.333
Dutch, French, Americans

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.200
, and Taiwanese tycoons

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.233
have flocked to this battlefield.

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:39.566
They competed fiercely, ruthlessly calculating and

00:00:39.566 --> 00:00:42.100
battling it out on the island for over 30 years, fighting to

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.433
the death.

00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:44.833
Some became legends, while

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.366
others were eliminated in disappointment.

00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:47.633
Hello everyone, I'm Fat Cat.

00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:49.500
Today, let's talk about this.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.600
Now, the first question

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.500
is: who started this war?

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:58.133
In 1988

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.733
, a company called Makro

00:00:59.733 --> 00:01:01.000
quietly arrived in Taiwan.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.800
What was the background of this company?

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.533
Behind the scenes of Makro

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:08.233
's success is the Dutch SHV Group, a hidden tycoon family that

00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:09.433
made its fortune in coal trading in the 19th century.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.766
Makro's

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:12.233
timing was impeccable;

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.400
Taiwan was booming at the time, with

00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:17.366
exports and real estate prices soaring,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.100
social wealth rapidly accumulating,

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.400
and everyone

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.000
eager to spend their money

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.500
. Makro was eyeing this lucrative market

00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:25.966
, but they were also clever enough

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.000
not to enter alone. Instead, they

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.233
partnered with Zhang Guoan, one of the founders of Sanyang Group and known as

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:32.366
the "Taiwanese Fish King" Fengqun

00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:34.966
, and Charoen Pokphand Group,

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.033
owned by the Xie family of Thailand's CP Group.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:38.533
This brought a completely new business model

00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:39.366
to Taiwan.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.533
In late 1989, the first Makro

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:43.966
officially opened in the Bade Industrial Zone of Taoyuan. Upon opening

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.766
, it

00:01:44.766 --> 00:01:46.133
completely bewildered

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.100
many Taiwanese.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:47.700
Why?

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.500
Because

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.433
there were requirements

00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:51.900
to buying things at this store : you had to get a membership card

00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.700
, and this card couldn't be obtained casually;

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.100
you had to have

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.966
proof of company registration.

00:01:57.233 --> 00:01:58.000
Walking into the store,

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.133
people were even more confused:

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.766
shelves reached the ceiling,

00:02:00.766 --> 00:02:02.366
and forklifts

00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:03.566
moved around right next to you. Children

00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:05.566
under 120cm tall were simply stopped

00:02:05.566 --> 00:02:07.366
at the door

00:02:07.366 --> 00:02:08.533
for fear of being hit by falling objects.

00:02:08.766 --> 00:02:09.366
So,

00:02:09.366 --> 00:02:12.566
it wasn't a shopping mall at

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:14.033
all; it was a

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.733
cold, impersonal logistics warehouse.

00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:17.566
The goods weren't sold retail;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.700
everything was sold by the box

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.200
or by the dozen.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.133
Based on the Dutch experience,

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.900
this kind of wholesale business targeting small vendors

00:02:24.933 --> 00:02:26.900
didn't usually have much foot traffic.

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:28.566
But they never imagined

00:02:28.566 --> 00:02:30.566
they would underestimate the Taiwanese people's

00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:31.766
fervor for low prices.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.800
At its peak,

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.166
Makro's six stores

00:02:34.166 --> 00:02:35.933
could generate 22 billion

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.700
NTD in sales annually. The Taipei Neihu store alone

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.700
could reach a daily turnover of 45 million NTD,

00:02:40.733 --> 00:02:42.533
earning it the nickname "King of Stores."

00:02:42.533 --> 00:02:44.766
So, what made Makro so successful

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.100
? It's simple

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.700
: extreme efficiency.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:49.133
The industrial area had cheap land,

00:02:49.133 --> 00:02:50.100
combining warehouse and store spaces

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.333
without unnecessary decorations.

00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:52.333
Bulk turnover

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:54.733
—all to keep prices down.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.700
This had its advantages and disadvantages.

00:02:56.966 --> 00:02:58.966
In that era of newly abundant resources,

00:02:58.966 --> 00:03:00.633
consumers could tolerate the inconvenience

00:03:00.633 --> 00:03:02.300
of traveling long distances,

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.933
getting membership cards, and carrying boxes home

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.766
for cheap prices . But people have...

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.033
When people started to feel

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.200
that driving an hour

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.433
to carry a box of unfinished canned goods

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:12.733
was torture, Makro

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.733
's blind spot was exposed.

00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:16.300
Almost simultaneously,

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.400
another local powerhouse, secretly

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.366
laying the groundwork, couldn't wait any longer.

00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:24.833
News of Makro's booming opening in 1989

00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:26.400
quickly reached

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.533
the ears of Kao Ching-yuan, the "Smiling Buddha"

00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:30.366
of the Tainan clique . However, he was unimpressed.

00:03:30.366 --> 00:03:32.433
A completely new business model landing in Taiwan?

00:03:32.433 --> 00:03:33.566
That was child's play.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.833
In Taiwan's retail industry,

00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:36.166
if a business was profitable,

00:03:36.166 --> 00:03:37.166
there was no

00:03:37.166 --> 00:03:38.400
reason for Uni-President not to get involved.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.900
In fact, two years earlier,

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.033
he had gone to France

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:42.666
and reached an agreement

00:03:42.666 --> 00:03:43.600
with the founding family of Carrefour.

00:03:43.633 --> 00:03:44.800
The French would hold 60%

00:03:44.833 --> 00:03:45.900
and Uni-President 40%.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.233
Even the Chinese name, "家乐福"

00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:49.633
(Jia Le Fu), was given by Kao Ching-

00:03:49.633 --> 00:03:51.833
yuan . The French meaning was "crossroads."

00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:52.700
Kao Ching-yuan

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:53.933
thought it was all nonsense;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.133
Taiwanese people wouldn't understand.

00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:57.700
He changed it to "家乐福" based on a homonym

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.300
and added the phrase "

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.133
家家快乐又幸福" (May every family be happy and blessed )

00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:03.800
. In one sentence, he made this foreign business more relatable. Uni-President, leveraging its past success

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.633
with 7-Eleven... Carrefour

00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:07.900
's adept experience in "using foreign resources to make things happen"

00:04:07.966 --> 00:04:10.200
led them to open the first Carrefour in Asia

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.733
on Dashun Road in Kaohsiung.

00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:14.500
This opening directly hit Makro in the nutshell.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.033
Makro required company certification to enter, but

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.933
Carrefour had no barriers;

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.333
anyone, young or old, could push a cart in.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.900
Makro was located in a remote industrial area, but

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.566
Carrefour

00:04:25.566 --> 00:04:27.600
moved its store to the busiest street

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.500
corner in the city, allowing you

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:31.100
to conveniently buy everything you

00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:32.600
needed after work. Makro focused on goods

00:04:32.633 --> 00:04:34.800
and how to minimize costs,

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.500
while Carrefour focused on people

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.666
and how to make you

00:04:37.666 --> 00:04:40.000
comfortably open your wallet.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.000
These two completely different business philosophies

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.033
clashed head-on on the island of Taiwan,

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.200
resulting in fierce and brutal

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:46.966
competition

00:04:46.966 --> 00:04:47.933
. Makro's

00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:49.166
headquarters were highly centralized,

00:04:49.233 --> 00:04:51.233
and every store seemed to be produced

00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:52.366
on the same assembly line.

00:04:52.566 --> 00:04:54.700
The most infuriating weapon for its competitors

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:57.366
was their promotional

00:04:57.366 --> 00:04:59.766
materials, which offered discounts of 30-50%

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.166
on best-selling items , sometimes even at a loss. Back

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.766
then, when you walked into a Carrefour store,

00:05:03.766 --> 00:05:05.600
everyone was holding a flyer

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.600
and scanning the cheap items printed on it

00:05:07.766 --> 00:05:10.166
– that was the crushing power of industrial efficiency.

00:05:10.166 --> 00:05:12.566
But Carrefour didn't confront you head-on; instead,

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.233
they played the decentralization game.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.633
The head office delegated power to each store

00:05:16.633 --> 00:05:19.566
manager, who was like a guerrilla force operating close to the ground. Whoever

00:05:19.566 --> 00:05:20.566
was closest to the customers

00:05:20.566 --> 00:05:22.333
had the authority to change tactics at

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.733
any time. They would stock more of whichever vegetables sold well

00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:26.133
and adjust promotional prices for whichever time

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:28.033
it was crowded. One was a central army

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.900
with precise calculations and

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.500
strict discipline

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.166
; the other was a flexible,

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.933
mobile local force.

00:05:35.166 --> 00:05:37.366
These two seemingly diametrically opposed strategies

00:05:37.433 --> 00:05:38.933
quickly determined the winner.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.366
Carrefour first established a foothold in the south

00:05:41.366 --> 00:05:43.333
and then quickly marched north,

00:05:43.333 --> 00:05:46.133
conquering Nangang and Tianmu in Taipei,

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.400
and then planting its flag in Banqiao.

00:05:47.533 --> 00:05:50.033
Along the western corridor, they fought from south to north. By

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.133
1996,

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:52.000
the results were revealed:

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.366
Carrefour

00:05:53.366 --> 00:05:54.400
surpassed Makro in both

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.900
the number of stores and annual revenue,

00:05:55.933 --> 00:05:57.833
becoming the number one hypermarket in Taiwan.

00:05:57.833 --> 00:05:59.366
Makro, the pioneer who first brought the shopping cart

00:05:59.366 --> 00:06:01.233
to the island...

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.833
Less than 10 years after its opening, it was brought down.

00:06:03.833 --> 00:06:04.966
At that very moment,

00:06:04.966 --> 00:06:07.833
a local outsider who started in the textile and fabric business

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.300
watched the fierce battle between the two giants

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.700
with a cold laugh.

00:06:11.833 --> 00:06:13.933
He was ready to teach these foreigners

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.133
a lesson

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:16.633
using the most primitive, underworld methods.

00:06:16.633 --> 00:06:18.700
This man's name was Yin Yanliang.

00:06:23.166 --> 00:06:24.333
To

00:06:24.333 --> 00:06:26.166
talk about Yin Yanliang, we have to start

00:06:26.166 --> 00:06:27.600
with his father, the "King of Checkered Fabrics,"

00:06:27.733 --> 00:06:29.833
Yin Shutian. The Yin family crossed the sea to Taiwan in 1949 and

00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.733
became one of the top figures

00:06:31.733 --> 00:06:33.300
in the Shandong branch of Taiwan's textile industry.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.133
But Mr. Yin had a problem:

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.533
he had five daughters

00:06:36.533 --> 00:06:39.500
before finally having his only son, Yin Yanliang, in middle age.

00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:41.500
This young master was a spoiled brat,

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.500
one of the most notorious troublemakers in Taipei. He

00:06:44.566 --> 00:06:46.766
was expelled from four schools in junior high, causing trouble

00:06:46.966 --> 00:06:47.933
until he was 16. Finally

00:06:47.933 --> 00:06:48.966
, his father gritted his teeth

00:06:48.966 --> 00:06:51.133
and sent him to Changhua Jinde Junior High School

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.000
. The reformatory school that specifically took in delinquent teenagers—

00:06:54.366 --> 00:06:55.000
and

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.900
guess what happened

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:58.433
when he got in? He made a good friend there

00:06:58.433 --> 00:06:59.500
named Huang Shao-

00:06:59.766 --> 00:07:00.700
cen

00:07:00.733 --> 00:07:03.133
, nicknamed "Momo," a "landlubber." He was also the second leader of the Bamboo Union gang,

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:04.766
handpicked by Chen Chi-li.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:07.033
Also at Jin-de Middle School,

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:09.600
Yin Yen-liang was fortunate to meet a good teacher

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.766
who scolded him awake.

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.033
That person later became the Speaker of the Legislative Yuan,

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.133
named Wang Jin-pyng.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.233
From then on, Yin Yen-liang tamed his temper,

00:07:16.233 --> 00:07:17.166
resumed his studies,

00:07:17.166 --> 00:07:18.133
and got back on the right track.

00:07:18.433 --> 00:07:19.533
However,

00:07:19.533 --> 00:07:21.233
the ruthlessness he had developed from the streets

00:07:21.233 --> 00:07:22.200
remained in his bones.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.733
In 1976, Yin Yen-liang took over the family business.

00:07:24.733 --> 00:07:26.000
By the 1990s,

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.200
Taiwan's textile industry was declining.

00:07:28.233 --> 00:07:30.700
Seeing the booming success of hypermarkets

00:07:30.733 --> 00:07:34.233
, and having a dormant old textile factory in his possession

00:07:34.233 --> 00:07:35.033
, he thought,

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:36.600
why not give it a try?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.600
What if it works?

00:07:37.733 --> 00:07:40.166
In 1996, RT-Mart officially became

00:07:40.233 --> 00:07:43.700
... RT-Mart opened its first store in Pingzhen,

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.700
Taoyuan in 1997. Like Kao Ching-yuan, who had a highly

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.433
skilled manager , the "godfather of distribution,"

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:49.566
Hsu Chung- jen, Yin Yen-liang also had a trusted lieutenant

00:07:49.566 --> 00:07:50.733
named Huang Ming-tuan

00:07:51.033 --> 00:07:53.166
. Huang later led a team to the mainland

00:07:53.166 --> 00:07:55.800
, making RT-Mart a dominant force in the mainland retail market,

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.733
known as the "King of Land Warfare."

00:07:57.733 --> 00:07:59.166
However, in Taiwan,

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.166
they faced

00:08:00.366 --> 00:08:03.033
a battlefield of hellish difficulty.

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:05.566
At this time, Carrefour played its trump card: "

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:06.766
Everyday Cheap!

00:08:06.833 --> 00:08:07.700
" What does this mean?

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.366
It offers four price guarantees :

00:08:09.433 --> 00:08:10.233
instant price checks,

00:08:10.233 --> 00:08:11.333
price transparency,

00:08:11.366 --> 00:08:12.700
promotional price guarantees,

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:13.966
and a refund if you find a lower price elsewhere

00:08:13.966 --> 00:08:15.500
. In short, it guarantees you

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.700
'll get the lowest price in Taiwan.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:18.733
This move

00:08:18.733 --> 00:08:21.400
was designed to crush the declining Makro

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.300
and shut out newcomers like RT-

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.800
Mart.

00:08:24.833 --> 00:08:28.133
Now, facing the ultimate pressure from the mountain of capital... How did RT

00:08:28.133 --> 00:08:30.133
-Mart survive

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:32.200
and even drive foreign companies to the brink of collapse?

00:08:32.366 --> 00:08:34.900
Huang Ming-duan later said in an interview, "

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:35.966
Our method

00:08:35.966 --> 00:08:37.766
of purchasing operations learned from American

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:39.700
store design, European

00:08:39.833 --> 00:08:41.433
product selection, and mainland China.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:42.566
We went through a long and winding road,

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.000
but it all boils down to three words: localization."

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:46.233
What is localization? It's about

00:08:46.233 --> 00:08:47.433
thoroughly mastering fresh produce and

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.533
bringing the wet market into the supermarket.

00:08:49.633 --> 00:08:51.533
Taiwanese housewives buy groceries every day,

00:08:51.533 --> 00:08:53.933
drawn by the freshness

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.600
and the lively atmosphere of picking and choosing.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:56.766
But this approach

00:08:56.766 --> 00:08:57.700
has a problem:

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.566
high spoilage rates and low profit margins for fresh

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.166
produce . Therefore, others generally try to avoid it.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.400
RT-Mart, however, insists on offering a more comprehensive selection

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.800
of fresh produce than its competitors.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:08.100
To control spoilage and ensure freshness,

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.500
the staff in the fruit and vegetable section

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.100
is almost twice that of other stores.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.866
Therefore, RT-Mart

00:09:12.866 --> 00:09:15.166
treats fresh produce as its most stable source of customer traffic.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.700
Housewives come every day for everyday necessities like oil

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:17.600
, salt, soy sauce, and vinegar

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:18.533
. Pots and pans

00:09:18.533 --> 00:09:20.700
were easily stuffed into the shopping cart.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.233
An outsider to the fabric industry

00:09:22.233 --> 00:09:24.566
managed to secure

00:09:24.566 --> 00:09:26.700
the second-largest retailer in Taiwan, nestled between two powerful competitors,

00:09:26.733 --> 00:09:28.600
earning the nickname "Local Little Tyrant."

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.633
Just when they thought they

00:09:30.633 --> 00:09:31.666
could maintain their dominance through

00:09:31.666 --> 00:09:33.366
fierce competition with fresh produce and low prices,

00:09:33.366 --> 00:09:35.966
a fourth force entered the fray

00:09:35.966 --> 00:09:38.833
, and they were in a panic. Why

00:09:38.933 --> 00:09:40.733
? Because of a massive fire.

00:09:44.566 --> 00:09:47.600
On the morning of October 29, 1995, around 5 a.m.,

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.166
a major event occurred in Kaohsiung.

00:09:49.166 --> 00:09:50.833
The most profitable flagship store

00:09:50.833 --> 00:09:52.300
of the powerful department store group, Datong Department

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.033
Store, was suddenly

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:55.900
engulfed in flames for over 20 hours

00:09:56.133 --> 00:09:57.333
, completely reduced to ruins,

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:00.166
with direct financial losses exceeding NT$2 billion.

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:02.333
This fire destroyed the hard work of founder Wu Yaoting

00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:03.633
over 30 years

00:10:03.633 --> 00:10:06.700
and forced Wu Zhenhua, the eldest son of his second wife and then the department store's general manager,

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.433
to resign. On the brink of collapse,

00:10:09.433 --> 00:10:12.300
although the old patriarch Wu Yaoting had not yet abdicated

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.100
, the lifeblood of Ta Tung was severed,

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.200
and Japanese department stores were making a major southward

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.500
expansion. Under the watchful eyes of his strict father

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.600
and two elder brothers,

00:10:19.633 --> 00:10:21.566
Wu Zhenhua, who had returned from studying in the United States, knew that

00:10:21.566 --> 00:10:23.133
if he did not do something,

00:10:23.133 --> 00:10:25.233
his future position as heir apparent might be in jeopardy.

00:10:25.433 --> 00:10:28.266
Therefore, he decided to use his international retail connections made

00:10:28.266 --> 00:10:29.966
during his studies in the United States

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.200
to cross the Pacific Ocean and

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.133
bring Costco to Kaohsiung for a joint venture.

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:36.400
However, bringing foreign investment to Taiwan was not easy.

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.533
The Wu family's vast commercial land

00:10:38.533 --> 00:10:40.633
was jointly owned by the three brothers.

00:10:40.633 --> 00:10:42.766
Any sale or lease

00:10:42.766 --> 00:10:44.800
of any piece of land required the approval of all three brothers.

00:10:44.833 --> 00:10:46.633
Wu Zhenhua wanted to divert land

00:10:46.633 --> 00:10:48.600
and invest huge sums of money in a joint venture with Americans.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.733
He not only had to convince his father, who was still shaken by the fire,

00:10:51.733 --> 00:10:53.366
but also the elders of the family.

00:10:53.366 --> 00:10:55.233
Navigating the complex web of

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.533
vested interests , he had to gamble

00:10:57.566 --> 00:10:59.033
to successfully take over Tatung Department Store.

00:10:59.166 --> 00:11:00.800
On January 18, 1997,

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.166
the first Costco in Taiwan

00:11:02.166 --> 00:11:04.333
opened on Zhonghua 5th Road in Kaohsiung.

00:11:04.366 --> 00:11:06.533
However, it didn't have a successful opening

00:11:06.633 --> 00:11:08.633
. Costco required members

00:11:08.633 --> 00:11:09.533
to pay a

00:11:09.533 --> 00:11:12.233
fee, a ridiculous logic

00:11:12.233 --> 00:11:14.333
that Taiwanese consumers simply couldn't accept.

00:11:14.566 --> 00:11:16.366
The then-Taiwan general manager, Zhang Sihan,

00:11:16.366 --> 00:11:18.800
had to fly to the Seattle headquarters every year

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:19.766
to report on the losses.

00:11:19.766 --> 00:11:20.933
Meanwhile, Wu Zhenhua in Taiwan

00:11:20.933 --> 00:11:23.333
faced

00:11:23.333 --> 00:11:25.933
immense criticism within the family for his perceived pro-foreignism and squandering of the family fortune.

00:11:26.133 --> 00:11:28.833
Yet, they made an extremely tough decision

00:11:28.833 --> 00:11:29.733
to persevere

00:11:29.733 --> 00:11:32.166
, using a low-margin 14%

00:11:32.166 --> 00:11:34.833
trial-and-error strategy and an unconditional return policy

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:37.300
as the core tools for breaking into the market.

00:11:37.333 --> 00:11:39.800
This approach remained consistent. In 2001,

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:40.966
the fifth year of

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:42.366
Costco's success, the Kaohsiung store became profitable.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.566
Since then, its performance has maintained double-digit growth annually .

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.100
Relying on its exceptionally high average transaction value and sales per square meter,

00:11:48.166 --> 00:11:49.966
Costco Taiwan's ranking on global lists has skyrocketed

00:11:49.966 --> 00:11:52.200
at an astonishing pace.

00:11:52.433 --> 00:11:53.833
The Taichung Nantun store,

00:11:53.833 --> 00:11:57.000
in particular, has consistently held the title of Costco's top-ranked store globally.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.400
Costco Taiwan boasts nearly 4 million members,

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.000
meaning one in five Taiwanese

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.733
is a Costco member, with

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:05.000
a renewal rate as high as 90%

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:06.500
, also ranking first globally.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.233
Zhang Sihan, who was criticized in the US every year,

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:10.633
was later

00:12:10.633 --> 00:12:12.200
appointed President of the Asia-Pacific region by

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.900
the US headquarters , managing 70 stores and 29,000 employees across Asia.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.766
Meanwhile

00:12:17.766 --> 00:12:20.766
, Wu Zhenhua, the son of the second wife,

00:12:20.766 --> 00:12:21.966
firmly

00:12:21.966 --> 00:12:24.200
held onto the core power of the department store and retail sector during the asset division after the old leader's death.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.566
In June 2022,

00:12:25.566 --> 00:12:27.566
the US headquarters, in an effort to regain control,

00:12:27.566 --> 00:12:30.300
offered the Wu family an astronomical sum of

00:12:30.333 --> 00:12:31.600
US$1.05 billion, which

00:12:31.633 --> 00:12:33.133
Wu Zhenhua couldn't refuse.

00:12:33.133 --> 00:12:34.433
This deal brought his Tatung

00:12:34.433 --> 00:12:37.766
Group a staggering NT$31.2 billion overnight

00:12:37.766 --> 00:12:40.033
, creating

00:12:40.033 --> 00:12:42.000
one of the most classic business battles

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:45.700
in Taiwanese retail history . However, just as Costco achieved legendary status in the early 2000s,

00:12:45.766 --> 00:12:47.566
some others couldn't withstand the pressure.

00:12:49.033 --> 00:12:51.166
In 2003, just after the Lunar New Year,

00:12:51.166 --> 00:12:53.533
the Taiwanese retail industry was hit by an unexpected earthquake

00:12:53.533 --> 00:12:55.500
in the early spring chill.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.500
The pioneer, Makro, suddenly announced

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.733
the closure of all six of its branches across Taiwan.

00:12:59.733 --> 00:13:02.800
From its high-profile entry in 1989 to this moment of closure,

00:13:02.833 --> 00:13:03.966
a full 14 years

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.433
had passed. Its pursuit of extreme efficiency

00:13:05.733 --> 00:13:06.933
by choosing locations in industrial areas,

00:13:06.933 --> 00:13:08.933
its insistence on requiring a membership card for entry

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.233
, and its increasingly blurred product positioning

00:13:11.233 --> 00:13:12.900
all became its fatal flaws.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.566
But if you think this was just

00:13:14.566 --> 00:13:16.533
a tragedy for Makro alone

00:13:16.566 --> 00:13:17.800
, you're underestimating

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:19.966
the ferocity of the Taiwanese retail market.

00:13:19.966 --> 00:13:22.566
This was merely the prelude to the industry's twilight.

00:13:22.733 --> 00:13:24.133
Backed by the Far Eastern Group and

00:13:24.133 --> 00:13:26.533
having previously partnered with a French giant, Alimama...

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:28.333
With stores across Taiwan shrinking

00:13:28.333 --> 00:13:30.333
and closures becoming increasingly common, losses

00:13:30.333 --> 00:13:32.500
dragged down the parent company's financial statements.

00:13:32.633 --> 00:13:33.733
Even

00:13:33.733 --> 00:13:36.200
the behemoth Taiwan Sugar Corporation, with its vast land

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:37.633
holdings and aggressive expansion

00:13:37.633 --> 00:13:39.300
, struggled for several years before

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.233
quietly abandoning its mess

00:13:40.466 --> 00:13:42.333
and exiting the market . A long list of names has been

00:13:42.333 --> 00:13:44.900
silently erased from Taiwanese memory,

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:47.333
such as Tesco, the British retail giant.

00:13:47.333 --> 00:13:49.500
When it entered the market, it

00:13:49.533 --> 00:13:51.033
boasted of investing heavily

00:13:51.033 --> 00:13:54.333
to open 20 mega-stores across Taiwan. However,

00:13:54.333 --> 00:13:55.233
it failed to adapt,

00:13:55.233 --> 00:13:57.433
opening only a paltry six stores.

00:13:57.633 --> 00:13:59.200
Everyone was asking

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.633
what happened.

00:14:00.633 --> 00:14:03.233
Why did these multinational giants with assets worth billions or tens of billions

00:14:03.233 --> 00:14:06.400
collectively collapse on this island,

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.466
as if under a curse?

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.800
The answer lies not in the stores themselves,

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.033
but in Taiwan's social structure.

00:14:13.033 --> 00:14:14.733
One of the most important reasons

00:14:14.733 --> 00:14:16.000
is the declining birth rate.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.700
These three words may sound like

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.633
a dry demographic term,

00:14:19.866 --> 00:14:21.100
but in the retail industry,

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:23.333
they represent a significant factor. The disaster that struck at the heart of the problem:

00:14:23.333 --> 00:14:25.000
Over the past 30 years,

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.833
Taiwanese families have become increasingly smaller.

00:14:26.833 --> 00:14:28.666
What were once lively extended families

00:14:28.666 --> 00:14:30.833
have shrunk to two- or three-person households.

00:14:30.933 --> 00:14:32.700
The bulky packages that symbolized

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.800
affluence and sophistication in the 1980s

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.366
have become an invisible burden that

00:14:36.366 --> 00:14:37.900
modern people simply can't carry

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.633
or finish.

00:14:39.933 --> 00:14:40.700
After the tide receded,

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.633
a chilling sound

00:14:42.633 --> 00:14:44.266
emerged from the darkness:

00:14:44.266 --> 00:14:46.033
the surviving behemoths of capital.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.366
A more brutal storm of mergers and acquisitions

00:14:48.366 --> 00:14:50.200
quietly began.

00:14:51.333 --> 00:14:54.133
The first behemoth to launch a ruthless devouring spree

00:14:54.133 --> 00:14:55.233
was Carrefour.

00:14:55.266 --> 00:14:56.533
First, it acquired Tesco in the UK

00:14:56.533 --> 00:14:58.033
, then swallowed Taiwan Sugar Corporation

00:14:58.033 --> 00:15:00.000
, and most unexpectedly,

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.666
in 2020, it spent NT$3.2 billion

00:15:02.666 --> 00:15:04.600
to swallow up

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:06.833
Wellcome Supermarket, a Hong Kong-funded brand

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.900
that had been operating in Taiwan for over 30 years,

00:15:08.933 --> 00:15:10.400
along with its more than 100 stores.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.933
Hearing this, you might find it strange,

00:15:12.933 --> 00:15:14.700
since we've been discussing

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.900
hypermarkets all day. Was this a war among hypermarkets?

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.100
Why would Carrefour, then the leading hypermarket chain,

00:15:19.133 --> 00:15:21.133
lower itself to compete with

00:15:21.133 --> 00:15:23.100
a bunch of small supermarkets on every street corner?

00:15:23.466 --> 00:15:25.000
The reason was a

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.133
name that would haunt Carrefour's dreams

00:15:27.133 --> 00:15:27.633
.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:30.666
By then, the powerful Carrefour had realized

00:15:30.666 --> 00:15:32.033
it was being

00:15:32.033 --> 00:15:34.433
slowly worn down by those small supermarkets on every street corner.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.400
Only by establishing hundreds of top-tier stores

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:37.533
and extending its reach

00:15:37.533 --> 00:15:40.533
 

00:15:40.533 --> 00:15:42.933
into the capillaries of communities throughout Taiwan could it have a chance of winning in a head-to-head battle with PX Mart

00:15:43.133 --> 00:15:44.933
. A year later, in October 2021,

00:15:44.933 --> 00:15:45.933
PX Mart, which Carrefour

00:15:45.933 --> 00:15:48.233
had been guarding against day and night, also made its move.

00:15:48.233 --> 00:15:50.700
Relying on its early years of lending money to people at Taipei's Erxin

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:53.066
and its close dealings with Zhang Zhongqi in Taichung,

00:15:53.066 --> 00:15:54.833
it acquired a welfare center for military personnel

00:15:54.833 --> 00:15:57.266
and civil servants , as well as land converted from government offices to residential land.

00:15:57.266 --> 00:15:58.900
I'll discuss that in a separate article later. Anyway,

00:15:59.033 --> 00:16:02.066
Lin Minxiong, who was playing dumb to take advantage of the situation, announced that PX

00:16:02.066 --> 00:16:04.433
Mart would spend NT$11.5 billion

00:16:04.833 --> 00:16:08.066
to directly buy out nearly 96% of RT-Mart's shares.

00:16:08.066 --> 00:16:10.800
The local little tyrant RT-Mart had thus bid farewell

00:16:10.933 --> 00:16:13.100
. Such a large move by

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.433
PX Mart

00:16:14.433 --> 00:16:15.500
directly challenges

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:17.066
Uni-President's market position . In 2022, Uni-President spent

00:16:17.066 --> 00:16:18.500
NT$30.2 billion

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.833
to acquire 100% of Carrefour Taiwan's shares.

00:16:21.833 --> 00:16:24.133
Thus, the French brand, which had been around for over 30 years

00:16:24.133 --> 00:16:26.066
, could only silently prepare

00:16:26.066 --> 00:16:28.433
to pack its bags and withdraw from the Asian market

00:16:28.466 --> 00:16:29.233
. The

00:16:29.233 --> 00:16:31.700
30-year-long saga of hypermarkets has come to a complete end. Only

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.800
the three most formidable forces in Taiwan remain

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.666
on this battlefield.

00:16:36.666 --> 00:16:38.266
These three forces combined

00:16:38.333 --> 00:16:40.333
have already captured over 80% of the market share,

00:16:40.433 --> 00:16:42.000
effectively dividing up

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.066
the entire Taiwanese retail landscape.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:46.633
So, is the war over? No. For

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:47.666
the past 30 years,

00:16:47.666 --> 00:16:49.666
everyone has been fighting for prime locations and

00:16:49.666 --> 00:16:50.633
large stores.

00:16:50.633 --> 00:16:52.100
But where is the next battlefield?

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:53.433
In your and my mobile phones. In

00:16:53.433 --> 00:16:54.433
May 2024,

00:16:54.433 --> 00:16:57.000
PX Mart's digital membership surpassed 10 million. Following this,

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.900
Lin Min-hsiung launched electronic payment services, and the number

00:17:00.266 --> 00:17:02.200
of users instantly exceeded 6 million.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.600
Meanwhile , Uni-President's One... The Points ecosystem,

00:17:04.633 --> 00:17:06.500
also leveraging thousands of

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.300
7-Eleven stores across Taiwan, has woven a vast network

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:10.233
with over 19 million members.

00:17:10.233 --> 00:17:11.333
In September 2025,

00:17:11.333 --> 00:17:13.033
Uni-President incorporated Carrefour, which it had just acquired,

00:17:13.033 --> 00:17:14.733
into this network

00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:15.433
, effectively

00:17:15.433 --> 00:17:17.633
bringing all consumers in Taiwan under its control

00:17:17.633 --> 00:17:18.933
. The battlefield has shifted;

00:17:19.266 --> 00:17:21.066
they're now vying for your data, your lifestyle habits

00:17:21.066 --> 00:17:23.466
, and the instinctive urge to open your phone's app

00:17:23.466 --> 00:17:25.333
every time you pull it out. No matter

00:17:25.333 --> 00:17:27.266
how large the retail stores are

00:17:27.266 --> 00:17:28.333
, they can't

00:17:28.333 --> 00:17:29.233
compete with the click of

00:17:29.233 --> 00:17:30.866
your thumb. The focus has shifted

00:17:30.866 --> 00:17:32.933
from who offers the best price to who understands you best,

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.266
from who's closest to you

00:17:34.266 --> 00:17:35.833
to who can retain you.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.200
The retail stores remain the same; what

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.300
changes is the winning strategy of each new generation of players.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:41.866
This is the true story of this 30-year war.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.666
RT-Mart has become Daquanlian,

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.200
and Carrefour's name will eventually

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.700
disappear from Taiwanese soil.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.933
Yin Yanliang has passed away.

00:17:49.033 --> 00:17:49.833
So, the next time

00:17:49.833 --> 00:17:51.833
you push that big shopping cart

00:17:51.833 --> 00:17:53.833
, pull out your phone to scan the code and pay,

00:17:54.066 --> 00:17:56.066
you might remember this episode.

00:17:56.066 --> 00:17:59.233
You're not just shopping at a supermarket or hypermarket

00:17:59.266 --> 00:18:00.166
; you're experiencing an entire

00:18:00.166 --> 00:18:02.200
epitaph that no one has written for them.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.800
30 Years of Taiwan Hypermarkets:

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:04.600
Thank you everyone.

